###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table I test MAEs are in kcal/mol/atom, which has no unit individual; they are kept with unit null and the unit in the label. Charge MAEs (e/atom, Table I) are not energy/force metrics.
# - Geometry-optimisation energies, IP and EA (Table II), reaction-path profiles (Figs. 5-6) and the charge-separation example (Table III) are property comparisons.
# - The descriptor is described as 'a variant of SOAP' and the implementation as built on TensorMol; neither is stated as the method bpopNN derives from, so no derived_from edge is recorded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/xie2020.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

